# Database & Migration Rules
# Applies to: SQL scripts, schema changes, database configuration

---

## Current State

> **⚠️ NO MIGRATION TOOL** - This project uses Spring SQL initialization, NOT Flyway/Liquibase.
> Scripts run on EVERY startup. HSQLDB is in-memory - ALL DATA LOST on restart.

---

## SQL Script Locations

```
src/main/resources/db/
├── hsqldb/
│   ├── initDB.sql      # Schema creation
│   └── populateDB.sql  # Sample data
├── mysql/
│   ├── initDB.sql
│   └── populateDB.sql
└── postgresql/
    ├── initDB.sql
    └── populateDB.sql
```

---

## CRITICAL RULES

### Rule 1: Update ALL Three Database Scripts
When modifying schema, **ALWAYS update all three database folders**:
- `db/hsqldb/initDB.sql`
- `db/mysql/initDB.sql`
- `db/postgresql/initDB.sql`

### Rule 2: Use Correct Auto-Increment Syntax
```sql
-- HSQLDB (default)
id INTEGER IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY

-- MySQL
id INT NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY

-- PostgreSQL
id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY
```

### Rule 3: Create Indexes on Foreign Keys
```sql
CREATE INDEX pets_owner_id ON pets (owner_id);
CREATE INDEX visits_pet_id ON visits (pet_id);
```

### Rule 4: Table Creation Order
Foreign keys must reference existing tables. Order in `initDB.sql`:
1. Parent tables first (owners, types, vets, specialties, users)
2. Child tables after (pets, vet_specialties, roles)
3. Grandchild tables last (visits)

---

## Naming Conventions

### Tables
```sql
-- Lowercase, plural
CREATE TABLE owners (...)
CREATE TABLE pet_types (...)
CREATE TABLE vet_specialties (...)  -- Junction tables: entity1_entity2
```

### Columns
```sql
-- Lowercase, snake_case
first_name VARCHAR(30)
birth_date DATE
owner_id INTEGER NOT NULL
created_at TIMESTAMP
```

### Indexes
```sql
-- Pattern: table_column
CREATE INDEX owners_last_name ON owners (last_name);
CREATE INDEX pets_name ON pets (name);
```

### Foreign Key Constraints
```sql
-- Pattern: fk_child_parent
ALTER TABLE pets ADD CONSTRAINT fk_pets_owners 
  FOREIGN KEY (owner_id) REFERENCES owners (id);
```

